  "heading": "\\inclusion.order:on{U}",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{inclusion order on the power set of }U",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\inclusion.order:on{U}]\nDefines: R is \\partial.order:on{\\power.set:of{U}}\nwhen: U is \\set\nexpresses:\n. forAll: A, B \"in\" \\power.set:of{U}\n  then:\n  . have: R(A, B)\n    iff: A \\:subset?:/ B\n. exists: E \"in\" \\power.set:of{U}\n  suchThat:\n  . E = \\empty.set\n  . forAll: A \"in\" \\power.set:of{U}\n    then: R(E, A)\n. exists: T \"in\" \\power.set:of{U}\n  suchThat:\n  . T = U\n  . forAll: A \"in\" \\power.set:of{U}\n    then: R(A, T)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"inclusion order on the power set of $U?$\"\n. description: \"Subset inclusion is a partial order on $\\mathcal{P}(U)$, with\n                the empty set as its least element and $U$ as its greatest\n                element.\"\nId: \"ff6d7e2f-1927-4d30-b771-34ea8726711c\"",
